ich a sheet takes exactly one","name":"Terrain Paper · the texture law"},{"path":"05-terrain-paper/the-card.html","group":"05 · Terrain Paper","viewport":"1000x480","subtitle":"Terrain's card, and Field Glass inverted for a light ground: warm haze light at the top and dense at the bottom, under a bright frosted rim. Type and icons always WHITE and etched. White rim at .45, b","name":"The card · the frost plate"},{"path":"06-roadbook-paper/contract.html","group":"06 · Roadbook Paper","viewport":"700x300","subtitle":"Adopted ✅ — ships in the live scoring tool. Terrain Paper reads; Roadbook Paper runs the numbers","name":"Contract · Roadbook Paper"},{"path":"07-broadcast-on-air/approved-boards.html","group":"07 · Broadcast On-Air","viewport":"700x420","subtitle":"The newest approved designs — curtain standings and fullscreen day results, from the live overlay","name":"Approved 2025 boards"},{"path":"07-broadcast-on-air/contract.html","group":"07 · Broadcast On-Air","viewport":"700x330","subtitle":"The origin — the 2025 overlay in the wild. Slightly transparent (≈80% panel fill ✅), never blurred, generously rounded; red means on-air here and nowhere else","name":"Contract · Broadcast On-Air"},{"path":"07-broadcast-on-air/element-kit.html","group":"07 · Broadcast On-Air","viewport":"700x360","subtitle":"The overlay's structural elements extracted for reuse: rb-* stays opaque and on-air; fg-* is the glass evolution","name":"Element kit — on-air & Field Glass"},{"path":"07-broadcast-on-air/raceline-exact.html","group":"07 · Broadcast On-Air","viewport":"700x300","subtitle":"Lifted verbatim from the curtain footer master, at three crops — use these shapes, don't redraw them","name":"The RaceLine — exact shapes"},{"path":"07-broadcast-on-air/rail-fitment.html","group":"07 · Broadcast On-Air","viewport":"700x540","subtitle":"Read from the curtain footer: the chassis rail, the RaceLine livery stripe, smooth fitment — and their glass & flat translations","name":"The RaceLine & 